{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 / Stage 3 experiment log, probes 2–5:\n\nGold-context control: ran the same model, system prompt, six criteria, response schema, and temperature with repository tools disabled and complete evidence supplied directly. It returned valid complete JSON in 7 seconds using 507 output tokens under a 1,024-token cap. This rejects the schema/finalizer and legitimate verdict size as the primary cause.\n\nValid criterion-isolation runs (the harness narrowed both initial context and show_ticket, correcting an earlier invalid attempt): criterion 1 PASS in 8 responses/11 tool calls/758 final tokens; criterion 2 PASS in 8/11/695; criterion 3 PASS in 51 responses/68 tools/~2.59M cumulative input tokens; criterion 5 PASS in 36/46/~1.29M; criterion 6 hit raw max_tokens at a 1,024 cap but PASSed at 4,096 in 15 responses/24 tools/1,387 final tokens. Criterion 4 was pathological at 4,096: 66 responses, 117 tool calls, ~3.35M cumulative input tokens, one identical search repeated 14 times (13 consecutively), followed by a cap-filling 199-line non-JSON response with no schema keys and raw provider reason max_tokens. This localizes the aggregate failure to unbounded per-criterion exploration/termination drift rather than ticket size or a uniformly oversized verdict.\n\nPrompt perturbation control: added affirmative finite-state termination wording for criterion 4. It still ran 50 responses/81 tool calls/~2.59M cumulative input tokens and filled 4,096 output tokens with 129 lines of non-JSON prose. Prompt wording alone is therefore insufficient.\n\nExecutable boundary control: a temporary PrepareTools hook hid repository tools after run_step > 16. Exploration stopped at 17 responses/31 tools, but the exhausted agent emitted unparseable prose and its structured retry emitted only eight tokens. This confirms an executable evidence-gathering bound is effective, while also showing that the long-running history cannot reliably recover the structured-output contract; finalization must use a fresh bounded turn over compact evidence.\n\nAll probes preserved fail-closed behavior; none converted truncation or malformed output into PASS."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785180002993584001,"uuid":"538a0bbb-74ae-4895-b90d-ab8227b02ae3"}